{"title":"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Quick_and_Easy,_using_larger_triangles)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Quick and Easy, using larger triangles)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The degree measure of angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/3/cc3d87ddc15f303c48dcb5e245523d226f95fbe3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(12); draw((0,0)--(20,0)--(1,-10)--(9,5)--(18,-8)--cycle); draw(arc((1,-10),(1+19/sqrt(461),-10+10/sqrt(461)),(25/17,-155/17),CCW)); draw(arc((19/3,0),(19/3-8/17,-15/17),(22/3,0),CCW)); draw(arc((900/83,-400/83),(900/83+19/sqrt(461),-400/83+10/sqrt(461)),(900/83 - 9/sqrt(97),-400/83 + 4/sqrt(97)),CCW)); label(rotate(30)*&quot;$40^\\circ$&quot;,(2,-8.9),ENE); label(&quot;$100^\\circ$&quot;,(21/3,-2/3),SE); label(&quot;$110^\\circ$&quot;,(900/83,-317/83),NNW); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,0),NW); [/asy]\" width=\"425\" height=\"302\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c7267e08cdeeb4b2ab3f7ac0e6197d645e14a8d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 20 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 30 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 35 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 40 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Angle-chasing using the small triangles:\n</p><p>Use the line below and to the left of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/3/ef3e8d51e7dfd1c3badcecdf2a277836c2ab649a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$110^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> angle to find that the rightmost angle in the small lower-left triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/9/e1972afe5272870f8d04664ccf415da947cd7434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180 - 110 = 70^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"125\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Then use the small lower-left triangle to find that the remaining angle in that triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f99c88e20cfcb8e09f1b4e93ecf29a42432c7d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180 - 70 - 40 = 70^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"156\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Use congruent vertical angles to find that the lower angle in the smallest triangle containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31adfcb608f857dff15cc5fa7ea0c327e8dc65ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />.  \n</p><p>Next, use line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to find that the other angle in the smallest triangle containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92cf7a626a3bc88dbcea2cc286baee0d1cc76487.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180 - 100 = 80^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"125\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>The small triangle containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31adfcb608f857dff15cc5fa7ea0c327e8dc65ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> angle and an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec5a68a3382ed121445e64488834a165dbe0bd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> angle.  The remaining angle must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/f/22fc3b48f483efb7538398862be3b6d260fde3ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180 - 70 - 80 = \\boxed{30^\\circ, B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"192\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Quick_and_Easy.2C_using_larger_triangles.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Quick_and_Easy,_using_larger_triangles)\">Solution 2 (Quick and Easy, using larger triangles)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Quick and Easy, using larger triangles)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The third angle of the triangle containing the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b19d9486c9b7645405202c0869ec43682a65bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> angle and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3388936ca5d53b685a625b9baac877382e278a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/7/ff76402411d1f65fdd728a284250630070cfa5df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ - 100^\\circ - 40^\\circ = 40^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"188\" height=\"13\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the third angle of the triangle consisting of the found <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3388936ca5d53b685a625b9baac877382e278a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> angle and the given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/3/ef3e8d51e7dfd1c3badcecdf2a277836c2ab649a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$110^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> angle. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c12816ae7fe5ff2416f3216bb92e6b3b1800f93d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ - 110^\\circ - 40^\\circ = 30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"188\" height=\"13\" /> angle, and so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/3/0a3515270044c86944732a0827eb4c4ac3bf75f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{30^\\circ, \\textbf{B}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"59\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/suaYxFnoU6E?t=99\">https://youtu.be/suaYxFnoU6E?t=99</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_.5B.F0.9F.94.A5Fast_and_Easy.F0.9F.94.A5.5D\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/X_SbFalrsV8?si=BLdIghVBvHNMmEIn\">https://youtu.be/X_SbFalrsV8?si=BLdIghVBvHNMmEIn</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8\" title=\"1999 AMC 8\">1999 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.